# Findings reviewed and accepted, by fingerprint.
#
# Fingerprints rather than path or regex allowlists, deliberately. A rule
# like "ignore anything under tests/" would also hide a real credential
# pasted into a test tomorrow, which is a likely way for one to get
# committed. Each line here is one specific string at one specific commit,
# looked at by a person, and anything new in the same file still fails.
#
# Format: <commit>:<path>:<rule>:<line>

# "Uses the token = abc123def456"
#
# A parameter in the test suite for NOVA's own secret detector. The test
# feeds looks_sensitive() a list of strings that look like credentials and
# asserts every one is refused before it can reach the memory store. The
# string has to look like a secret or the test proves nothing -- so the
# scanner flagging it is the test working, one layer up.
